==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.21.1|
* Elemental Ailments other than Freeze are no longer discarded if their duration is lower than 300ms.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.19.0|
* The Brittle Ailment now grants up to +6% chance to critically strike afflicted enemies (previously +15%) and now has a default value of +2% (previously +5%).
* Fixed an issue where the effects of Brittle and Sapped ground were not affected by Ailment effect.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.0|
* [[Scorch]] and '''Brittle''' (alternate ailments for Fire and Cold damage respectively) have both had their maximum effects raised. 
: '''Brittle''' now increases the chance to critically strike an afflicted enemy by up to 15% (from 10%).
: Scorch, '''Brittle''' and Sap now all have a base duration of 4 seconds (from 2).
}}
{{Version history table row|3.9.0|
* We've added an Ailment Threshold to monsters. In the great majority of cases, the Ailment Threshold matches the monster's Maximum Life. It primarily differs for especially high-life monsters (such as The Shaper), where the threshold is reduced to allow ailments to be applied with hits that wouldn't ordinarily reach the required Life thresholds.
* The alternate ailments Sap, Scorch and '''Brittle''' have a slightly different calculation as they have lower caps on their magnitudes.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.6.0|
* Now grants up to +10% chance to critically strike afflicted enemies. This chance is further increased by sources of increased Critical Strike Chance, whereas previously, as the result of a bug, it was not.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.5.0|
* Introduced to the game.
* Updated the reminder text for Ailments to include the '''3 new Ailments'''.
* (Stated in patch preview) Hits have up to +20% Critical Strike Chance against '''Brittle''' Enemies, based on the Cold Damage of the Hit which inflicted '''Brittle''', for 2 seconds.<ref name=Bex/>
}}
{{Version history table end}}

